---
layout: base.njk
title: My Blog
pagecss: <link rel="stylesheet" href="/resources/css/blog.css">
pagejs: <script src="/resources/js/blog.js" defer></script>
---

<div id="blog-page">
    <header class="blog-header pop-in">
        <h1 class="blog-title">The Cutting Room</h1>
        <p class="blog-subtitle">My insights from behind the scenes <small style="font-size: 0.9rem;">(that should probably be cut)</small></p>
    </header>

    <div class="categories-strip pop-in">
        <a href="/blog/" class="category-tag active">All</a>
        <a href="/blog/tags/post-production/" class="category-tag">Post-Production</a>
        {# <a href="/blog/tags/production/" class="category-tag">Production</a> #}
        <a href="/blog/tags/writing/" class="category-tag">Writing</a>
        <a href="/blog/tags/sound-design/" class="category-tag">Sound Design</a>
        <a href="/blog/tags/film-tv/" class="category-tag">Film & TV</a>
        <a href="/blog/tags/the-walking-dead/" class="category-tag">The Walking Dead</a>
    </div>

    <div class="blog-grid">
        {% set latestPosts = collections.blogPosts | slice(0, 4) %}
        {% for post in latestPosts %}
        <article class="blog-post {% if loop.index0 == 0 %}featured{% endif %} pop-in">
            <div class="post-meta">
                <div class="post-meta-tags">
                    {% for tag in post.data.tags %}
                    <a href="/blog/tags/{{ tag | slugify }}/" class="post-category {{ tag | slugify }}">{{ tag | titleCase }}</a>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
                <div class="post-meta-info">
                    <span class="post-date">{{ post.data.date | dateFormat }}</span>
                    <span class="reading-time">{{ post.templateContent | readingTime }} min read</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            {% if loop.index0 == 0 %}
            <h2><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></h2>
            {% else %}
            <h3><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></h3>
            {% endif %}
            <p class="post-excerpt">{{ post.data.excerpt }}</p>
            <a href="{{ post.url }}" class="read-more">Read More →</a>
        </article>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="blog-navigation pop-in">
        <div class="nav-buttons">
            <a href="/blog/posts/" class="nav-button primary">
                <span class="nav-icon">📚</span>
                <span class="nav-text">
                    <strong>View All Posts</strong>
                    <small>Browse {{ collections.blogPosts.length }} articles</small>
                </span>
            </a>
            <a href="/blog/tags/" class="nav-button secondary">
                <span class="nav-icon">🏷️</span>
                <span class="nav-text">
                    <strong>Browse by Tags</strong>
                    <small>Explore {{ collections.blogTags.length }} categories</small>
                </span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="blog-intro pop-in">
        <h2>Why "The Cutting Room"?</h2>
        <p>In a standard production, the cutting room is where the entire project comes together. Where all assets and ideas get mended together before shipping the final product out. It is the last time in the process where things can truly remain unfiltered. <u>This</u> is my cutting room. The only spot where you can take a glimpse at my unfiltered thoughts and hopefully learn something about what makes filmmaking such a compelling art form.</p>
    </section>
</div>
